<===> README.md
A space always separates a media query or selector from its block, also if
it ends with an escape that is terminated by a space (`\9 `), which gives two
spaces in expanded output, like dart-sass.
<===>
================================================================================
<===> media_feature/input.scss
@media (a: b\9 ) {
  c {d: e}
}
<===> media_feature/output.css
@media (a: b\9 ) {
  c {
    d: e;
  }
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> media_interpolated/input.scss
@media #{screen\9} {
  a {b: c}
}
<===> media_interpolated/output.css
@media screen\9  {
  a {
    b: c;
  }
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> media_type/input.scss
@media screen\9 {
  a {b: c}
}
<===> media_type/output.css
@media screen\9  {
  a {
    b: c;
  }
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> nested_selector/input.scss
a {
  b\9 {
    c: d;
  }
}
<===> nested_selector/output.css
a b\9  {
  c: d;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> selector/input.scss
selector\9 {
  a: b;
}
<===> selector/output.css
selector\9  {
  a: b;
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> selector_list/input.scss
a, b\9 {
  c: d;
}
<===> selector_list/output.css
a, b\9  {
  c: d;
}
